  "question": "For the matrix $M=\\begin{bmatrix} 0 & x & y \\\\ x & 0 & z \\\\ y & z & 0 \\end{bmatrix}$, evaluate $|M|$ if $x=1$ and $y=2$, $z = 3$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "With $x=1$, $y=2$, $z=3$:<br /><br />$|M| = \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\end{vmatrix}$<br /><br />Expand along the first row:<br /><br />$= 0 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix} 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\end{vmatrix} - 1 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\end{vmatrix} + 2 \\cdot \\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 \\end{vmatrix}$<br /><br />$= 0 - 1(1\\times0 - 2\\times3) + 2(1\\times3 - 2\\times0)$<br /><br />$= 0 - 1(0-6) + 2(3-0)$<br /><br />$= 0 - (-6) + 6 = 6 + 6 = 12$.",
